<!--
THIS FILE IS THE EDITABLE SOURCE (a `.tmpl`, not itself a served page) --
a generic starting point. Copy it to site/privacy.html.tmpl (untracked,
never overwritten by an upgrade -- see README.md "Static-site pages") and
replace every REPLACE-ME marker with your own real controller/contact/
processor details before publishing.

The retention_months / canceled_retention_months placeholders below are
filled in automatically by app/site_render.py from settings.toml's
[privacy] values, so this legal page's retention numbers can never
silently drift from the actual, enforced config -- leave those two
placeholders exactly as they are, only edit the surrounding wording.
-->

<p class=MyTitle>Privacy Policy</p>

<p><b>Controller:</b> REPLACE-ME-YOUR-NAME-OR-ORGANIZATION, contact
<a href="mailto:REPLACE-ME@example.org">REPLACE-ME@example.org</a>.</p>

<p><b>What is collected:</b> when you book a session, your name and
email address are used to confirm your spot, contact you about that
specific session, and let you cancel it. If you use the self-service
booking tool you also choose a 6-digit code to manage your own bookings;
only a salted hash of it is stored, never the code itself. REPLACE-ME:
describe here whether any other information is collected (e.g. health
disclosures) -- this template assumes none.</p>

<p><b>Why (legal basis):</b> your consent, given when booking, and where
relevant the need to fulfil the booking you asked for (Art. 6(1)(a)/(b)
GDPR). REPLACE-ME: confirm this matches your actual setup.</p>

<p><b>Who else sees it (processors):</b> REPLACE-ME: list every
third-party service that processes registrant data on your behalf (email
provider, calendar provider, hosting provider, ...) and whether each has
a signed data-processing agreement with you.</p>

<p><b>How long it's kept:</b> booking records are kept for up to
{{!retention_months}} months after the session date ({{!canceled_retention_months}} months if canceled), then
automatically deleted. You can delete your own account and booking
history at any time from the booking tool's "my bookings" page, or by
emailing <a href="mailto:REPLACE-ME@example.org">REPLACE-ME@example.org</a>
-- your email address is then irreversibly hashed and cannot be linked
back to you.</p>

<p><b>Cookies:</b> no advertising or tracking cookies. Only a
strictly-necessary session cookie is used while you're logged into the
booking or "my bookings" page, which doesn't require consent under EU
ePrivacy rules. REPLACE-ME: confirm this matches your actual setup if
you've added anything else to the site.</p>

<p><b>Your rights:</b> access, correction, deletion, restriction,
objection, and data portability regarding your own data, plus the right
to complain to your local data protection authority. Contact
<a href="mailto:REPLACE-ME@example.org">REPLACE-ME@example.org</a> for
any of these.</p>

<p><i>REPLACE-ME: this template is a starting point, not legal advice --
see README.md's disclaimer. Confirm with your own legal/compliance
judgement (or counsel, if the stakes warrant it) that this page actually
describes what your deployment does before publishing it.</i></p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p><a href="/index.html">&larr; Back to home</a></p>

</body>
